{"name":"Iridescent","hex":"#3a5b52","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"iridescent","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Producing a display of lustrous, rainbow-like colors; prismatic.","Brilliant, lustrous, or colorful."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iridescent"}],"entries":[{"title":"Iridescent (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Iridescent\" is a song by American rock band Linkin Park. It was announced as the band's third US, fourth international and overall final single from their fourth studio album, A Thousand Suns, which was released on September 14, 2010. A music video for the song was directed by Joe Hahn, the band's turntablist."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c1/24_Iridescent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iridescent_(song)","wikidata":"Q19990"},{"title":"Iridescent (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Iridescent is the fourth studio album by American metalcore band Silent Planet. The album was released on November 12, 2021, through UNFD and Solid State Records. It was co-produced by Drew Fulk, Daniel Braunstein and guitarist Mitchell Stark. It is the last album to feature the band's bassist and clean vocalist Thomas Freckleton before he left the band in June 2023 due to wanting to spend more time with his family and having a fusion in his spine which had only gotten more painful over the years. It is also the band's first album to feature clean vocals from Garrett Russell and Mitchell Stark, and the first to include explicit language."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/37/SilentPlanetIridescent.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iridescent_(album)","wikidata":"Q108795697"},{"title":"Iridescence","blocks":[{"text":"Iridescence is the phenomenon of certain surfaces that appear gradually to change colour as the angle of view or the angle of illumination changes. Iridescence is caused by wave interference of light in microstructures or thin films. Examples of iridescence include soap bubbles, feathers, butterfly wings and seashell nacre, and the mineraloid opal. Pearlescence is a related effect where some or most of the reflected light is white. The term pearlescent is used to describe certain paint finishes, usually in the automotive industry, which actually produce iridescent effects."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Soap_Bubble_-_foliage_background_-_iridescent_colours_-_Traquair_040801.jpg/330px-Soap_Bubble_-_foliage_background_-_iridescent_colours_-_Traquair_040801.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iridescence","wikidata":"Q957208"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/RedSquare_%28pixinn.net%29.jpg/500px-RedSquare_%28pixinn.net%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/RedSquare_%28pixinn.net%29.jpg/500px-RedSquare_%28pixinn.net%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The single remix of \"Iridescent\" was performed live at Red Square (pictured) in Moscow.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARedSquare_(pixinn.net).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Dieselrainbow.jpg/500px-Dieselrainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Dieselrainbow.jpg/500px-Dieselrainbow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fuel on top of water creates a thin film, which interferes with the light, producing different colours. The different bands represent different thicknesses in the film. This phenomenon is known as thin-film interference. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADieselrainbow.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Iridescent_biofilm_on_a_fishtank.JPG/500px-Iridescent_biofilm_on_a_fishtank.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Iridescent_biofilm_on_a_fishtank.JPG/500px-Iridescent_biofilm_on_a_fishtank.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An iridescent biofilm on the surface of a fish tank diffracts the reflected light, displaying the entire spectrum of colours. Red is seen from longer angles of incidence than blue.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIridescent_biofilm_on_a_fishtank.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Black_pearl_and_his_shell.jpg/500px-Black_pearl_and_his_shell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Black_pearl_and_his_shell.jpg/1280px-Black_pearl_and_his_shell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Black_pearl_and_his_shell.jpg/500px-Black_pearl_and_his_shell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The pearlescent shell of a black-lip pearl oyster","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_pearl_and_his_shell.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Iridescent_begonia.jpg/120px-Iridescent_begonia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Iridescent_begonia.jpg/250px-Iridescent_begonia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6